{"at":"2026-10-13T12:54:31.974Z","tool":"submit_plan","args":"{\"issue\":99002,\"plan\":\"# Text properties\\nupdate C-001: the text starts at line height \\\"Loose\\\"; after the font family change, the line height is still 1.5 and \\\"Loose\\\" stays highlighted\\ncreate TC-1: \\\"Line height\\\" presets \\\"Tight\\\", \\\"Normal\\\" and \\\"Loose\\\" on a multi-line text\\ncreate TC-2: \\\"","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:44.416Z","tool":"save_changes","args":"{\"issue\":99002,\"content\":\"Scope: line height control for text (issue 99002), desktop browsers plus the 375 px mobile layout. Exact line heights are read from the number field of the \\\"Line height\\\" control in the properties panel. Agreed values: range 0.8 to 2.5, step 0.05, presets \\\"Tight\\\" = 1.0, ","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:47.453Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"The \\\"Line height\\\" control in the text properties panel applies to the whole text element and offers presets \\\"Tight\\\" = 1.0, \\\"Normal\\\" = 1.25 and \\\"Loose\\\" = 1.5, plus a number field that accepts a typed value from 0.8 to 2.5 in steps of 0.05.\",\"source\":\"PO answe","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:49.103Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"In the \\\"Line height\\\" field, values below 0.8 become 0.8, values above 2.5 become 2.5, values between steps round to the nearest 0.05, a comma decimal such as \\\"1,5\\\" is read as 1.5, and empty or non-numeric input keeps the previous value.\",\"source\":\"PO answer 3 on","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:50.752Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"New text keeps its font's own line height until a line height is chosen, after which the last chosen value is the default; a text whose line height was set keeps it when its font family changes, while a never-set text follows the new font's line height.\",\"source\":\"P","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:52.452Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"The \\\"Line height\\\" control is shown when a text, a shape with text, an arrow with a label or a sticky note is selected or the Text tool is active, not for shapes without text, images or an empty selection; with several texts at different line heights no preset is h","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:54.053Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"bound-text\",\"fact\":\"A larger line height makes a shape holding text grow taller with the same width and a smaller one lets it shrink back; an arrow label stays at the middle of the arrow; a sticky note's auto-fit takes line height into account and never shows the label larger than the picke","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:55:55.439Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"files-and-export\",\"fact\":\"Line height survives a page reload, a saved .excalidraw file, PNG and SVG export and live collaboration; paste styles, copies and library items carry it and undo/redo restore it; older Excalidraw versions are out of scope.\",\"source\":\"Approved answers 11 and 12 in t","outcome":"ok"}
